@startuml
title Manage POS / IoT Devices (System Admin – Swimlane Activity Diagram)

|System Admin|
start
:Log in to admin portal;

|Admin Portal|
:Send login credentials\nto Wallet System for authentication;

|Wallet System|
:Verify admin username/password\nand check role = System Admin;
if (Valid System Admin?) then (yes)
  :Return "Login success" to Admin Portal;
else (no)
  :Return "Login failed";
endif

|Admin Portal|
if (Login failed?) then (yes)
  |System Admin|
  :See error message;
  stop
else (no)
  :Display Admin Dashboard;
endif

|System Admin|
:Select "Manage POS / IoT devices" menu;

|Admin Portal|
:Request current device list\nfrom Wallet System;

|Wallet System|
:Fetch device list from DB
(id, type, location, service unit, status);
:Return device list to Admin Portal;

|Admin Portal|
:Display device table\n(POS, Gate In/Out, Kiosk, etc.);

|System Admin|
:Choose action on devices;

if (Add new device?) then (yes)
  :Click "Add new device";

  |Admin Portal|
  :Show "Create device" form
  (Device ID, name, type,\nlocation, service unit, status);

  |System Admin|
  :Fill in device information:
  - Device ID (unique)
  - Device type (POS / PARKING_GATE_IN / PARKING_GATE_OUT / KIOSK / OTHER)
  - Location (Building, Gate, Canteen)
  - Service unit (Canteen A, Parking B, Library…)
  - Initial status (ACTIVE / INACTIVE);
  :Click "Save";

  |Admin Portal|
  :Send "Create device" request\nto Wallet System with input data;

  |Wallet System|
  :Validate device data:
  - Device ID not duplicated
  - Valid device type
  - Valid service unit reference;
  if (Validation OK?) then (yes)
    :Insert new device record into DB;
    :Write audit log (who, what, when);
    :Return "Create success" to Admin Portal;
  else (no)
    :Return "Create failed + error reason";
  endif

  |Admin Portal|
  if (Create success?) then (yes)
    :Show success message\nand refresh device list;
  else (no)
    :Show error message\nfor System Admin;
  endif

else (no)
  if (Edit existing device?) then (yes)
    |System Admin|
    :Select a device from list;
    :Click "Edit";

    |Admin Portal|
    :Display current device info\nin editable form;

    |System Admin|
    :Modify fields (e.g. location,\nservice unit, display name);
    :Click "Save changes";

    |Admin Portal|
    :Send "Update device" request\nto Wallet System;

    |Wallet System|
    :Validate changes;
    :Update device record in DB;
    :Write audit log (who, what, when, before/after);
    :Return success/failure;

    |Admin Portal|
    :Show update result to System Admin;
    :Refresh device list;

  else (no)
    if (Activate / Deactivate device?) then (yes)
      |System Admin|
      :Select device from list;
      :Click "Activate" or "Deactivate";

      |Admin Portal|
      :Ask for confirmation (optional);
      :Send "Change device status" request\nto Wallet System;

      |Wallet System|
      :Update device status (ACTIVE/INACTIVE);
      :Write audit log (status change);
      :Return result;

      |Admin Portal|
      :Show result and refresh list;

      note right
        Devices with status INACTIVE
        must not be allowed to initiate
        or approve payment transactions.
      end note

    else (no)
      |System Admin|
      :No changes, just view device list;
    endif
  endif
endif

|Wallet System|
:Expose updated device configuration\nto POS/IoT gateways (sync step\nmay be periodic or on-demand);

|System Admin|
:Logout from admin portal;
stop
@enduml
